get=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T13:47:14-07:00","id":1144530,"title":"","content":"Orbiting around DC these days. Grew up in West Virginia and Pennsylvania.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T04:39:28-07:00","id":1144704,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4m originally from Cologne, Germany. I\u00b4d say it\u00b4s one of the most laidback cities in germany. <br /> Studied for 5 years in Bonn, stayed in South America for a year and moved to Berlin 2 years ago. <br /> <br /> So I never lived in a part where &quot;Lederhosen&quot; were commonplace.<br /> I was always amused how especially the old WoD books depicted Germany. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T06:10:30-07:00","id":1144726,"title":"","content":"Galicia, a land, region, what-have-you on the north-west of Spain. Beautiful if treacherous coasts, green forests and plenty of rain, usually. Great food, great drinks and a somewhat melancholic if party-hard folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:08:57-07:00","id":1144777,"title":"","content":"I live in a town called Savona, not much far from Genoa, in the northern part of Italy but still close right over the sea. My town is a small one but still nice. It's big but not too big, nature is close and we have some cool stuff to see. Gave the world a pair of popes and tried to become important in the Renaissance but failed, plus some other historical trivia.<br /> <br /> Weather is alright and so is the place, but we're essentially a nothing in the big scheme of things. Not exactly a town famous for its social activities either. Finding people who like the CoD here is kinda impossible and the groups of WoD fans are quite grumpy and closed to new people, so things are not easy on that side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 09-28-2017, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:37:37-07:00","id":1144789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1144777#post1144777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I live in a town called Savona, not much far from Genoa, in the northern part of Italy but still close right over the sea. My town is a small one but still nice. It's big but not too big, nature is close and we have some cool stuff to see. Gave the world a pair of popes and tried to become important in the Renaissance but failed, plus some other historical trivia.<br /> <br /> Weather is alright and so is the place, but we're essentially a nothing in the big scheme of things. Not exactly a town famous for its social activities either. Finding people who like the CoD here is kinda impossible and the groups of WoD fans are quite grumpy and closed to new people, so things are not easy on that side.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here in Roanoke, the few WoD fans here utterly hate nWoD/CoD. I'm sort of an exception as I started with Requiem before switching to Masquerade because everyone else was playing that instead. All the other RPG fans in my area tend to hate WoD and CoD due to either associating it with Twilight for some reason or because of the off-putting antics of the Roanoke WoD LARP scene at the time.<br /> <br /> Also, they prefer Revised Masquerade with the metaplot, while I prefer 1e/2e Masquerade without the metaplot (though V20 is also excellent as well). <br /> <br /> TL;DR You have my sympathies when it comes to finding a good WoD/CoD group. If you're interested in either Requiem 1E or Lost 1E, I could run a Play-By-Post for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T01:56:30-07:00","id":1145135,"title":"","content":"Denmark, a town called Esbjerg on the West Coast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T02:17:23-07:00","id":1145142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1144789#post1144789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Here in Roanoke, the few WoD fans here utterly hate nWoD/CoD. I'm sort of an exception as I started with Requiem before switching to Masquerade because everyone else was playing that instead. All the other RPG fans in my area tend to hate WoD and CoD due to either associating it with Twilight for some reason or because of the off-putting antics of the Roanoke WoD LARP scene at the time.<br /> <br /> Also, they prefer Revised Masquerade with the metaplot, while I prefer 1e/2e Masquerade without the metaplot (though V20 is also excellent as well).<br /> <br /> TL;DR You have my sympathies when it comes to finding a good WoD/CoD group. If you're interested in either Requiem 1E or Lost 1E, I could run a Play-By-Post for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as many Wod or CofD fans in Savannah as one would think. There is a WoD larp group, but i don't have the larp rules so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T07:30:56-07:00","id":1145219,"title":"","content":"Moved to Chambersburg, PA in 2002, after 24 years on the Mississippi Gulf Coast, bringing with me a fair number of WoD, \u00c6on-verse (as we called it then) and <b>Exalted</b> books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T11:10:20-07:00","id":1145304,"title":"","content":"I live in Longueuil, just under Montr\u00e9al but i was born in Granby (great zoo there btw). All in the province of Qu\u00e9bec in Canada.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T06:06:49-07:00","id":1145502,"title":"","content":"Although I'm from Barcelona, cyrrently I'm living in Tuxtla Guti\u00e9rrez, Chiapas, M\u00e9xico","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T11:23:53-07:00","id":1145577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1144518#post1144518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">San Diego, California. It's heaven on earth except for the skyrocketing rent and the fact that your choice of wildfire, megaquake, or military strike will someday wipe us off the map.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacramento, California. This is the state capital of California. We used to have major air force bases, but those were privatized in the early 1990s after a round of Cold War base closures. The economy has never really recovered in that range, despite efforts to grow our technology base. Essentially, we are a hinterland of San Francisco and the Bay Area, though we do have a lot of health care, education and government jobs. Rental unit construction has been limited, almost as much as Detroit's and Detroit is seen as a bad city. Exacerbating that rental market has been restriction on building that was just lifted in the Natomas area and builders focusing on larger single-family homes, so that if you aren't making a ton of dough, your housing options are limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T13:07:40-07:00","id":1145615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1145577#post1145577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sacramento, California. This is the state capital of California. We used to have major air force bases, but those were privatized in the early 1990s after a round of Cold War base closures. The economy has never really recovered in that range, despite efforts to grow our technology base. Essentially, we are a hinterland of San Francisco and the Bay Area, though we do have a lot of health care, education and government jobs. Rental unit construction has been limited, almost as much as Detroit's and Detroit is seen as a bad city. Exacerbating that rental market has been restriction on building that was just lifted in the Natomas area and builders focusing on larger single-family homes, so that if you aren't making a ton of dough, your housing options are limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember going to Sacramento on a school trip as a kid and thinking it was a ghost city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T04:12:22-07:00","id":1145753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1145502#post1145502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I'm from Barcelona, cyrrently I'm living in Tuxtla Guti\u00e9rrez, Chiapas, M\u00e9xico</div> </div> </div> </div>El lugar de conejitos! &lt;3 <br /> How is your gaming situation there?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T22:05:24-07:00","id":1145980,"title":"","content":"It's almost inexistent. I've only have known one local that knew what a tabletop RPG was (and by interet, not in person). I almost prefered the reactions in Barcelona when people knew I played RPGs (in Spain there was the local equivalent of the U.S. Satanic Panic,but in the 90s).<br /> <br /> So I decided to create my own troupe with my University students (I am a History teacher), so I directed them Fall of the Camarilla. We almost dont play (not enough free time for me), but I'd like to direct them The Sundered World (Neolithic Mage The Awakening).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T16:42:00-07:00","id":1146844,"title":"","content":"T\u00e1pi\u00f3szecs\u0151, Hungary. <br /> <br /> It's a middle-sized town, or an -almost- small city near (45 minutes with train) to Budapest. I love the capital, with all my heart (it's really one of the most beautiful and history-ridden cities of the world, the centre with the Danube is even a World Heritage and rightfully so) with all of its scenes and cultural life and I went there for high school and I'm still going for participating in basically anything (for example, rpgs), but actually, I always liked to go home to the agglomeration more (okay, daily commuting still sucks). There's something for clean air, less buildings, less light pollution and having the woods practically at my backdoor...<br /> <br /> CofD (or rather, NWoD) never got a real foothold there (I mean Budapest, in my hometown I'm not sure there was more than a dozen rpg players at any time). Oh, sure, some people bought (some of) the books (including me), played some games, even tried a longer campaign. I'm sure there are groups out there playing it, but it's 90% WoD, tabletop and LARP both and mostly Vampire (revised got published in Hungarian, with supplements and novels, so it's not surprising), though plenty of people knows and plays the others too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T06:28:06-07:00","id":1148798,"title":"","content":"Now? Port St. Lucie, FL. Haven't gamed in a bit, though. Had a number of great gamers to play with over the last 15-20 years(I'm almost 40 now). Not many gamers left in my area and it's very difficult to find time; and I also find myself weening quite a bit from the Onyx Path model of games and the current political climate(injecting politics into everything). I know there have always been politics in gaming and culture stretching back two decades, but I also used a lot less sugar in my coffee than I do now. Escapism is not really an escape for me, anymore.<br /> <br /> Which is fine.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly capable of using my free time(and money) on other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T06:56:42-07:00","id":1148806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1148798#post1148798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now? Port St. Lucie, FL. Haven't gamed in a bit, though. Had a number of great gamers to play with over the last 15-20 years(I'm almost 40 now). Not many gamers left in my area and it's very difficult to find time; and I also find myself weening quite a bit from the Onyx Path model of games and the current political climate(injecting politics into everything). I know there have always been politics in gaming and culture stretching back two decades, but I also used a lot less sugar in my coffee than I do now. Escapism is not really an escape for me, anymore.<br /> <br /> Which is fine.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly capable of using my free time(and money) on other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds sad, that you lost your fun in gaming. But hobby do change, and interestingly you are still arround in the forums. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Interesting: For me the current Onyx Path games, are way more unpolitical than the WW stuff from the 90\u00b4s. But i guess when one comes to age one sees more politics in everything as we come to understand that very little is unaffected by politics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T08:23:25-07:00","id":1148826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1148806#post1148806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds sad, that you lost your fun in gaming. But hobby do change, <b>and interestingly you are still arround in the forums</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say I lost my fun in gaming. I...literally never said that.<br /> <br /> And these forums cover all editions, right? Including the ones I was so fond of years ago(and have most recently played). And I'm extremely curious in how new WW handles 5th edition(and so far, I'm pretty stoked for it). There's probably a dozen other reasons while I'm still around, besides those two important ones.<br /> <br /> And I'm always down with the &quot;punching up,&quot; down with the man, and fight the power feelings of the old WW books. The most recent ones, however, have much more added political and social baggage, IMO. <br /> <br /> Which, AGAIN, is great if that works for you. For me, not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T11:20:05-07:00","id":1148865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1148798#post1148798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now? Port St. Lucie, FL. Haven't gamed in a bit, though. Had a number of great gamers to play with over the last 15-20 years(I'm almost 40 now). Not many gamers left in my area and it's very difficult to find time; and I also find myself weening quite a bit from the Onyx Path model of games and the current political climate(injecting politics into everything). I know there have always been politics in gaming and culture stretching back two decades, but I also used a lot less sugar in my coffee than I do now. Escapism is not really an escape for me, anymore.<br /> <br /> Which is fine.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly capable of using my free time(and money) on other things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry you feel that way. I generally avoid putting politics in my games and if you're interested in a non-political old-school WoD game, I can help you out and start a play-by-post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T19:38:58-07:00","id":1148969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1148826#post1148826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I'm always down with the &quot;punching up,&quot; down with the man, and fight the power feelings of the old WW books. The most recent ones, however, have much more added political and social baggage, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Judging from what we know so far, I think V5 will be <i>more</i> political and even more leftist political, but maybe closer to the older editions' feel. I'm seeing a lot more anti-authoritarian themes right now than identity politics themes. Which is good in my book. Albeit I could be totally wrong, we'll see.<br /> <br /> Also, my problem with OPP's works never were the inclusion of identity stuff in the games. That was always a part of it and rightly so. But I didn't like how they sometimes changed the setting to fit it to certain contemporary politics, while toned down a lot of the old themes. Most of them are still pretty good books though and this whole thing is not always prevalent and at the forefront, but it totally soured me on, for example DAV20.<br /> <br /> Totally unrelated (maybe I'll open a new thread for it), but I'm pretty excited about LexOccultum right now. It seems to be a great WoD alternative, with an 18th century setting (woefully underused), the pictures are beautiful and oozes style and some vague Ravenloft-feel, while the rules are of a good ol' classic-style rpg's. What's not to love? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T07:27:37-07:00","id":1149088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1144328-world-of-darkness-and-the-world?p=1148969#post1148969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> LexOccultum right now. It seems to be a great WoD alternative, with an 18th century setting (woefully underused), the pictures are beautiful and oozes style and some vague Ravenloft-feel, while the rules are of a good ol' classic-style rpg's. What's not to love?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Never heard of it. I'll have to check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T11:53:58-07:00","id":1149488,"title":"","content":"Stockholm, Sweden here.<br /> <br /> My Exalted game is on hiatus while we are waiting to find out if one of the players still will be able to participate, but over the net, after she moves to another continent. Not sure the game will survive, but one can always hope. Other than that, all is quite on the gaming front.<br /> <br /> There are quite a bit of roleplayers over here, but finding a bunch of people that are both compatible game-style wise and schedule wise... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm actually considering giving video-chat based roleplay a chance after they change the ISP for the building in November.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T15:45:29-07:00","id":1149780,"title":"","content":"Hi maekkel; try to guess where im from...<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T09:39:59-07:00","id":1149939,"title":"","content":"Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, in the northwest of Spain. It's a small city of about 100.000 inhabitants, with many students, burocrats and clergy, and a a center o pilgrimage. Galicia is a rural country with disperse population, natural landscapes and a melancholic weather and people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2250,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","user":"Magus","date":". 10-16-2017, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-16T04:47:56-07:00","id":1150116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> 